 "notes": "Den Osse haven: the outer western harbour mole of Den Osse, with entries at the end of the pier and at the small shell beach west of it, a sandy plateau sloping to the 5/10/15 m contours with a basalt patch to the north-west, and the harbour mouth to the east where diving is not allowed. Shoreline and mole from OpenStreetMap; positions are approximate. The site coordinates sit in the marina about 500 m south-east; the drawing is placed at the real entries relative to them.",
